# One Ollama per line, `host:port` and optional nginx upstream flags. Copy to
# `backends` beside nginx.conf.tmpl. healthcheck.sh probes each address every
# minute; render.sh turns the whole line into nginx's upstream block. A backend
# on another machine is just its LAN address — but not one of kdocker2's own
# macvlan addresses (the host cannot reach those).
#
# Flags, after the address:
#   weight=N        share of receipts relative to the others (default 1)
#   backup          only used when no primary is up
#   max_fails=N     override the default passive check (max_fails=1)
#   fail_timeout=Ns override the default sideline period (fail_timeout=20s)
#
# The boxes are not equals, so plain least_conn is not what you want: kdocker3
# parses a receipt in ~3.4 s warm against kdocker2's ~6.7 s (#124). Weighted,
# the fast box takes the share it can actually turn around.
192.168.10.38:11434 weight=3     # kdocker3, Radeon AI PRO R9700 32 GB
127.0.0.1:11434                  # kdocker2, iGPU — slower, still useful
